Finally, let's learn how to determine a missing dimension of a triangular prism given its volume and some other dimensions.

For example, consider the triangular prism below (not drawn to scale). The volume of this triangular prism is [math]54\:\text{ft}^3.[/math] What is the length of the prism?

\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{pgfplots}
